course: dictionary
lesson: 11976
title: Celestial: of the sky and heaven
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: «Celestial» is an adjective. It has two main meanings. The first is to do with the sky or outer space, such as the stars, planets and moons. The second is to do with heaven, or something heavenly and very beautiful.
explain: «The astronomer studied the celestial bodies through her telescope.» Astronomers study things in space, so celestial bodies must be objects in space, like stars, planets and moons.
explain: «The choir sang with celestial music that filled the old church.» Here celestial means heavenly and very beautiful. The music is so lovely it seems to come from heaven. Ask yourself: is the writer talking about the sky, or about something beautiful? The clues in the sentence will tell you.
fact: «Celestial» means to do with the sky or outer space.
fact: «Celestial bodies» are objects in space, such as stars, planets and moons.
fact: «Celestial» can also mean heavenly, or very beautiful, as in «celestial music».
fact: The «celestial sphere» is an imaginary dome of the sky, used by astronomers to show where stars appear.
exercise: «The astronomer studied celestial bodies through her telescope.» What are celestial bodies? | Buildings in the city centre | *Objects in space, such as stars, planets and moons | Clouds made of cotton wool | Animals that live in the sea
exercise: «The choir sang with celestial music that filled the old church.» What does celestial mean here? | Sung in a hurry | *Heavenly and very beautiful | Made of wood | Very loud and noisy
exercise: Which of these is a celestial body? | A cup | A bicycle | A puddle | *A planet
test: Which word is closest in meaning to celestial, meaning heavenly? | *Heavenly | Tiny | Gloomy | Cold
test: Which sentence uses celestial to mean to do with the sky? | The baker made a celestial cake | The celestial dog ran across the field | *The telescope showed the celestial bodies in the night sky | The celestial music was played too loudly
exam: In astronomy, what is the celestial sphere used for? | To measure how heavy a rock is | To paint pictures of the sea | *To map where stars and planets seem to be in the sky | To bake bread for the class
